

**7. Error Function and Fresnel Integrals**

**Mathematical Properties**

**7.1. Error Function**

**7.1.1**

**erf** \(z\) = \(\frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}\int_{0}^{z}\!\!e^{-t^{2}}\!dt\)

**7.1.2**

**erfc** \(z\) = \(\frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}\int_{z}^{\infty}\!\!e^{-t^{2}}\!dt\) = 1\(-\)erf** \(z\)

**7.1.3**

**\(w(z)\) = \(e^{-t^{2}}\!\left(1\!+\!\frac{2i}{\sqrt{\pi}}\int_{0}^{z}\!\!e^{t^{2}}\!dt\right)\)**= \(e^{-t^{2}}\!\!\)erfc** \((-iz)\)

**7.1.2**

**the path of integration is subject to the restriction** \(\arg\,t\!\rightarrow\!\!\alpha\) **with** \(|\alpha|\!\!<\!\!\frac{\pi}{4}\) **as** \(t\!\rightarrow\!\!\infty\) **along the path.** \((\alpha\!=\!\!\frac{\pi}{4}\) **is permissible if** \(\mathscr{R}t^{2}\) **remains bounded to the left.)**

**Integral Representation**

**7.1.4**

\(w\) (\(z\)) = \(\frac{i}{\pi}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\frac{e^{-t^{2}}\!dt}{z\!-\!t}\) = \(\frac{2iz}{\pi}\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{e^{-t^{2}}\!dt}{z^{2}\!-\!t^{2}}\) (\(\mathscr{I}z\!>\!0\))

**7.1.5**

**erf** \(z\) = \(\frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}\sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{n}z^{2n+1}}{n!(2n\!+\!1)}\)

**7.1.6**

**7.1.7**

**w** \((z)\) = \(\frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}\sum\limits_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{2^{n}}{1\!\cdot\!3\,\cdot\, \ldots\,\,(2n\!+\!1)}\)\(z^{2n+1}\)

**7.1.8**

**For** \(I_{n-1}(x)\)**, see chapter **10. Symmetry Relations**

**7.1.9**

**erf** \((-z)\) = \(-\)erf** \(z\)

**7.1.10**

**erf** \(\widetilde{z}\) = \(\widetilde{\rm erf}\)\(z\)

**7.1.11**

**w** \((-z)\) = \(2e^{-t^{2}}\!\!-\!w(z)\)

**7.1.12**

**w** \((\widetilde{z})\) = \(\widetilde{w}(-z)\)